                                "text": "Another lawyer and well-known Shakespearian, Richard Grant White, says: \"No dramatist of the time, not even [Francis] Beaumont, who was the younger son of a judge of the Common Pleas, and who after studying in the Inns of Court abandoned law for the drama, used legal phrases with Shakespeare's readiness and exactness.[…]\""
